{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AghZiLJTvPAjWemeqEvtP2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019iEFLVRnEKogmCMQyfbLP9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/_project/paper/section7_conclusion_compressed.tex"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4957,"cache_read_input_tokens":36906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4957,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":39,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GXZppFwTASjrABhJ2fF4BU","session_id":"b35164d6-59ff-4dc9-a0a2-e7bd8feeacab","uuid":"fb47446b-f940-483b-9524-c82db4a499ec"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019iEFLVRnEKogmCMQyfbLP9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t% Section 7 — Discussion and Conclusion (compressed)\n2\t% Merges key discussion points with conclusion\n3\t% Full discussion paragraphs on low F1 practical significance and\n4\t% decoding-time vs. post-hoc enforcement moved to Appendix B.\n5\t\n6\t\\paragraph{Discussion.}\n7\t% exp_ids: phase2_scierc_full_s1 (CF=9.90%), phase2_scierc_grammar_only (CF=0.08%),\n8\t%          phase2_docred_full_s1 (CF=2.57%), llama_docred_full_s1 (CF=12.02%)\n9\tCross-field consistency (CF) violations are qualitatively different from domain/range violations: each individual triple remains type-valid, and only cross-triple consistency is broken when the same entity receives different types across relations.\n10\tThe dominant conflict pattern---\\emph{Generic}$\\leftrightarrow$\\emph{OtherScientificTerm} (60 of 245~affected entities on SciERC)---reflects genuine semantic ambiguity in the type system rather than a systematic method failure.\n11\tAblation evidence cleanly attributes CF to the semantic layer: grammar-only decoding yields CF\\,=\\,0.08\\%, matching the unconstrained baseline, while the full system reaches 9.90\\% on SciERC and 2.57\\% on DocRED (Qwen3-8B; Llama-3.1-8B exhibits 12.02\\% on DocRED), confirming that CF arises from per-relation independent enforcement where each relation's constraint mask is computed without access to type decisions made for other relations.\n12\t% exp_ids: phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_docred_full_s1, llama_docred_full_s1\n13\t%\n14\t% exp_ids: d012_bootstrap_ci (DocRED +0.50pp p<0.001, SciERC +0.13pp p=0.58),\n15\t%          phase0_docred_unconstrained (RV=29.66%), phase0_scierc_unconstrained (RV=1.39%)\n16\tThe divergence in F1 significance between DocRED ($+$0.50\\,pp, $p < 0.001$) and SciERC ($+$0.13\\,pp, $p = 0.58$) traces to grammar-layer elimination of out-of-vocabulary (OOV) relation names: the DocRED baseline exhibits an RV rate of 29.66\\%---5{,}189~predictions with OOV relation names, all counted as false positives---while SciERC's baseline RV is only 1.39\\% (24~OOV predictions), too few to produce a detectable F1 effect.\n17\t% exp_ids: phase0_docred_unconstrained, phase0_scierc_unconstrained\n18\tLlama-3.1-8B's lower baseline RV (16.03\\% vs.\\ Qwen's 29.66\\%) yields a smaller but directionally consistent improvement ($+$0.29\\,pp vs.\\ $+$0.50\\,pp), confirming that F1 gain magnitude is proportional to baseline OOV rate.\n19\t% exp_ids: llama_docred_unconstrained (RV=16.03%), llama_docred_full_s1 (R-F1 delta=+0.29pp)\n20\t% qwen_docred: RV=0.2966, R-F1 delta=+0.50pp\n21\t\n22\t\\paragraph{Contributions.}\n23\t% exp_ids: phase0_scierc_unconstrained, phase0_docred_unconstrained,\n24\t%          phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_docred_full, phase2_scierc_grammar_only,\n25\t%          llama_docred_full_s1, llama_docred_unconstrained\n26\tWe presented OntoCoDec, a framework that automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into token-level decoding constraints to enforce type validity at generation time.\n27\tWe conducted the first systematic study of ontological constraint violations in LLM-based IE, finding that violation severity is driven by constraint tightness $\\bar{\\tau}$ rather than ontology scale: SciERC ($\\bar{\\tau}{=}0.333$) and DocRED ($\\bar{\\tau}{=}0.842$) exhibit comparable DR rates (15.37\\% vs.\\ 18.46\\%) despite a 14$\\times$ difference in ontology size.\n28\tOur two-layer architecture---a grammar layer (XGrammar CFG) eliminating structural violations (RV, ET\\,$\\to$\\,0\\%) and a semantic layer (TypeConstraintProcessor) enforcing domain/range constraints---achieves 45--99\\% DR reduction across two models and two datasets while preserving extraction quality.\n29\t\n30\t\\paragraph{Limitations.}\n31\t% exp_ids: phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_full_s1,\n32\t%          phase2_scierc_grammar_only, llama_docred_full_s1, llama_docred_unconstrained\n33\tThe semantic layer introduces CF violations---up to 9.90\\% on SciERC (Qwen3-8B) and 12.02\\% on DocRED (Llama-3.1-8B)---a systematic consequence of per-relation independent enforcement that remains an open challenge; the grammar layer alone does not elevate CF (0.08\\%), confirming it is entirely attributable to the semantic layer.\n34\tConstrained decoding increases parse failure rates for some configurations: Llama-3.1-8B on DocRED shows 9.1\\% parse failures under full constraints versus 6.8\\% unconstrained, likely due to max-token truncation.\n35\tResults cover two models under zero-shot prompting only; integration with fine-tuned models has not been explored.\n36\t\n37\t\\paragraph{Future Work.}\n38\tGlobal entity-level type consensus during decoding---maintaining a shared entity registry across relations within an instance---offers the most direct path to resolving CF violations.\n39\tFurther validation with fine-tuned models, larger scales (quantized 70B-class), and non-English ontologies remains to be explored.\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GXZppFwTASjrABhJ2fF4BU","session_id":"b35164d6-59ff-4dc9-a0a2-e7bd8feeacab","uuid":"795b72ee-90ec-47f8-b4c8-3339aee9ab7a","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:43:16.820Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YTbDwgJvDNnHFE4G9XuQN7","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# OntoCoDec — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-14 20:43 UTC | 更新原因: 修正 Llama unconstrained DR 数据错误 (18.36%→26.07%) + 核心方向描述加 model-dependent + 补全近期任务\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\n两层约束解码（grammar + semantic）近完全消除 LLM-based IE 的本体类型违规，F1 impact model-dependent: neutral (SciERC) to positive (DocRED Qwen, +0.50pp p<0.001)。详见 paper_framing.md。\\\\n\\\\n## 当前阶段\\\\nResearch — **全部 20 个实验完成**（19 success, 1 killed）。进入论文修订收尾。目标 May 19 内部稿 → May 25 EMNLP ARR。\\\\n\\\\n## 实验完成度\\\\n- 总计: 20 个实验，19 success，1 killed，0 RUNNING\\\\n- SciERC 5-way ablation (Qwen): ✅\\\\n- DocRED 4-way ablation (Qwen): ✅\\\\n- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ (DR↓99.4%)\\\\n- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ (unconstrained DR=26.07%, full_s1 DR=2.55%, DR↓90.2%)\\\\n- Phase 0 violation landscape: ✅ SciERC + DocRED\\\\n- Post-hoc baseline: ✅ (D013 multi-dimensional framing)\\\\n- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ (entity filter bug fixed + re-verified)\\\\n- D011 ET fix (v2 checker): ✅ 全量重跑完成\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策摘要\\\\n- D014: Tightness scaling → 双因素 (tightness × model RV baseline)\\\\n- D013: Post-hoc framing → 不争 F1，多维对比 (recall + coverage + operational)\\\\n- D012: Bootstrap CI → SciERC neutral (p=0.58), DocRED significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001)\\\\n\\\\n## 活跃工作流 (May 14 ~21:30 UTC)\\\\n\\\\n### GPU 实验\\\\n（无 — 全部完成）\\\\n\\\\n### Agent 工作\\\\n- D014 修订指令在队列中等待执行（§5 tightness rewrite + cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion + limitations + placeholders）\\\\n- 前置 worker callbacks 处理中\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [ ] D014 §5 tightness claim 修订（tightness × RV baseline 双因素）— Agent 队列中\\\\n- [ ] Abstract/Conclusion E-F1 claim limitation（Qwen-specific）— Agent 队列中\\\\n- [ ] §5 Cross-model subsection（2×2 matrix table + narrative）— Agent 队列中\\\\n- [ ] Limitations expansion（CF 12.02% + parse failures 6.8%→9.1% + scope）— Agent 队列中\\\\n- [ ] [LLAMA-DOCRED-TBD] placeholder filling — Agent 队列中\\\\n- [ ] Discussion 段落更新（加入 Llama DocRED 数据）\\\\n- [ ] Bibliography 最终编译检查\\\\n- [ ] main.tex 集成 + 全文数字一致性终审\\\\n- [ ] May 19: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\nwestd-16980: cuda:0 + cuda:1 分配给本项目。当前空闲（全部实验已完成）。\\\\n\\\\n## Dream 后行动完成度 (6/6 ✅)\\\\n1. Post-hoc baseline — ✅ D013\\\\n2. Bootstrap CI — ✅ D012 (entity filter fix verified)\\\\n3. Related work 20+ refs — ✅ 42 entries merged\\\\n4. PICARD detailed comparison — ✅\\\\n5. CF/F1 discussion — ✅ discussion_paragraphs.tex\\\\n6. Variance estimates — ✅ bootstrap CI\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D014 | 2026-05-14 | Tightness scaling claim 修订：从单因素(tightness)改为双因素(ti | llama_docred_full_s1, llama_docred_unconstrained, phase2_docred_full_s1 |\\\\n| D013 | 2026-05-14 | Post-hoc baseline framing: 不以 F1 论高低，多维对比 (recall  | phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_docred_unconstrained, phase2_docred_full_s1 |\\\\n| D012 | 2026-05-14 | Bootstrap CI framing: 选 (B) 逐数据集报告 F1 significance | phase2_docred_full_s1, phase2_scierc_full_s1 |\\\\n| D011 | 2026-05-14 | 推翻之前 ET 计数口径决定——修正 ET triple-counting，每个 entity 只计 | phase2_docred_unconstrained, phase2_docred_semantic_only |\\\\n| D010 | 2026-05-14 | Dream 三档 Weak Reject (3/6) → 制定 6 项结构性补强计划：post-ho | llama_docred_full_s1, llama_docred_unconstrained, llama_scierc_full_s1 |\\\\n| D009 | 2026-05-14 | Llama-3.1-8B cross-model 验证升级为 should-have，SciERC- | phase2_scierc_full_s1, phase2_scierc_unconstrained |\\\\n| D008 | 2026-05-14 | 补跑 DocRED semantic_only 完成跨数据集全消融；论文写作提前至 DocRED 分 | phase2_docred_grammar_only, phase2_docred_full_s1, phase2_scierc_semantic_only |\\\\n| D007 | 2026-05-14 | S2 降级为架构 ablation，S1 为主推策略；标题去掉 \\\\\\\"Guaranteed\\\\\\\" 改 \\\\\\\"Ne | phase2_scierc_full_s2, phase2_scierc_full_s1 |\\\\n| D006 | 2026-05-14 | Phase 2 SciERC 核心结果确认：Full S1 DR -94% 且 F1 无损，CF v | phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_scierc_semantic_only, phase2_scierc_full_s1, mvp_phase0_docred_schema |\\\\n| D005 | 2026-05-14 | Phase 2 SciERC 核心结果确认：Full S1 DR↓94% F1无损，CF viola | phase2_scierc_unconstrained, phase2_scierc_grammar_only, phase2_scierc_semantic_only, phase2_scierc_full_s1 |\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 3780, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JPxrYGQ86xZhrQijzNu4k7","session_id":"b35164d6-59ff-4dc9-a0a2-e7bd8feeacab","uuid":"35522d28-d808-4834-a3f3-bda8315234a8","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:43:16.810Z"}
